<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">What is the six-engine analysis framework?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">The six-engine analysis framework systematically examines how your brand appears across major AI platforms including ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews, Perplexity, Claude, Copilot, and others to identify messaging inconsistencies and create alignment strategies.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">How long does it take to achieve consistent brand messaging across AI engines?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Initial improvements typically appear within 60-90 days, with full consistency achieved over 6-12 months. The timeline depends on the extent of current inconsistencies and the comprehensiveness of your implementation.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">What type of content works best for maintaining brand consistency?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Citable content with clear structure, authoritative information, and consistent terminology works best. This includes definitive company pages, decision-stage content, and structured data markup that AI engines can easily access and interpret.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">How often should I monitor brand messaging across AI engines?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">Monthly monitoring of key brand queries across major AI engines is recommended, with quarterly strategic reviews to assess overall messaging consistency and identify emerging issues or opportunities.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">What happens when AI engines provide incorrect information about my brand?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">When misrepresentation occurs, trace the source of incorrect information, strengthen authoritative content on those topics, and implement schema markup to provide AI engines with accurate, structured data about your brand.</p>
</div>
<div class="border-b border-white/10 py-6">
<h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#F8F8F8] mb-2">Can I use the same content strategy for all AI engines?</h3>
<p class="text-white/70">While core messaging should remain consistent, different AI engines have varying source preferences and response patterns. Advanced strategies involve platform-specific approaches while maintaining unified brand narrative.</p>
